# pyforge-atlas run-admission lock store (AD-23, admission.py). Sibling of the Kedro
# data root: when PYFORGE_ATLAS_DATA_ROOT=<repo>/data, locks land in <repo>/data.locks/
# (not under src/shared/packages/pyforge-atlas/, where the member .gitignore already
# ignores data.locks/). Zero-byte *.lock markers + optional *.holder.json sidecars;
# ephemeral — recreated on every kedro run, never commit.
data.locks/

# Repo-root Kedro data when PYFORGE_ATLAS_DATA_ROOT=<repo>/data (bootstrap chain default).
# Anchored to the repo root (Story 30.2 fix) -- an unanchored `data/` matches at ANY depth,
# silently swallowing every station's own package `data/` dir (pyforge-doctor, -steward,
# -warden, -marshal all ship real tracked files there, e.g. report-schema.json). Found live
# 2026-09-20: a newly added src/shared/packages/pyforge-doctor/.../data/docs-map-schema.json
# was invisible to `git add -A` -- present on disk, tracked nowhere, would have shipped in no
# build and silently degraded docs-currency to a permanent fail-open WARN.
/data/

# Claude Code harness runtime artifacts (session lock from ScheduleWakeup, etc.)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# headroom MCP wrapper's own per-process env-var ownership state (PID/port, never
# meaningful across a process restart)
.claude/.headroom_wrap_marker.json
.claude/.headroom_wrap_owners.json

# pyforge-marshal: advisory-lock sidecar files (Story 4.9, AD-42) --
# `marshal deploy promote`'s FsPort.acquire_advisory_lock creates
# `planning-artifacts/specs.lock` to serialize concurrent promotions;
# release_advisory_lock best-effort removes it, but a crashed holder can
# leave it behind (harmless -- its mere existence never blocks a later
# acquire, only a live flock hold does), so it's ignored rather than
# tracked either way.
_bmad-output/projects/*/planning-artifacts/specs.lock

# spec_surface_check.py --write-baseline (Story 12.5, DW-13-5-2/-3): the
# advisory-flock sidecar (deliberately never unlinked) and the atomic-replace
# temp file next to the committed baseline.
scripts/.spec-surface-baseline.json.lock
scripts/.spec-surface-baseline.json.tmp

# BMAD: personal config (user-scoped) and per-developer artifacts.
# Note: _bmad/custom/*.user.toml is already handled by _bmad/custom/.gitignore.
# Note: project-scoped planning-artifacts (PRDs, briefs, ADRs) are committed team artifacts.
# Note: project-scoped implementation-artifacts are gitignored (per-developer scratch).
_bmad/config.user.toml
_bmad/custom/.active-project
_bmad-output/projects/*/implementation-artifacts/
# Story 21.2 chain-regen run journals + orphan manifests (local scratch).
_bmad-output/projects/*/planning-artifacts/.chain-regen/
# ...and the same path as a SYMLINK. The trailing-slash rule above matches only
# real directories, so in a bmad-loop home — where `bmad-loop-worktree` creates
# implementation-artifacts as a Tier-3 BACKLINK to the main checkout — the path
# came back untracked, and `bmad-loop run` refuses to start on a dirty worktree.
# Every new loop home hit this on its first launch (found provisioning marshal,
# 2026-07-25). No trailing slash = matches the symlink too.
_bmad-output/projects/*/implementation-artifacts

# bmad-loop / upstream-tooling seam: root artifact dirs are LOCAL symlinks to the
# active project's dirs (re-point on `bmad-switch`; see docs/specs/bmad-loop-adoption.md)
_bmad-output/planning-artifacts
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts
_bmad-output/projects/*/.bmad-config.user.toml

# Junie: personal config (user-scoped) and per-developer artifacts.
.junie/

# kedro-viz session store / stats (prototypes/cf-atlas-kedro-viz; build/ is
# already covered by the global build/ rule above)
.viz/
.bmad-loop/runs/
.bmad-loop/cache/
# `bmad-loop clean`'s default (non---hard) sweep archives concluded runs here
# as .tar.gz rather than deleting them -- never listed alongside runs/cache/
# above, so it showed up as untracked cruft in every loop-home worktree and
# `bmad-loop run` refuses to start on a dirty worktree (found live 2026-08-13,
# pyforge-steward, after a routine `bmad-loop clean`).
.bmad-loop/archive/
# marshal writes its model-cost catalog sidecar beside the loop policy in every
# loop home (harness_bmadloop.py: _MODEL_COST_CATALOG_SIDECAR) and never
# removes it; untracked + not ignored it made `bmad-loop validate` report
# "git worktree is not clean" on the marshal home (steward prove-landed,
# 2026-09-06, 7/8 homes clean).
.bmad-loop/marshal-model-cost-catalog.json
# bmad-loop writes the story's HEAD commit hash to this file at the run-worktree
# root and never removes it. It has no in-repo producer or consumer (`grep -rn
# claude_hash` across scripts, hooks, .bmad-loop/ and settings finds neither), and
# it was NOT gitignored -- so the loop's own `git add -A` swept it into a merge
# commit and it rode onto loop/pyforge-scribe. Scribe's Story 1.2 review predicted
# exactly that ("any later `git add -A` automation would sweep it into a commit")
# and the prediction came true in the same run that made it; the entry is now
# DW-1-2-* in that project's tracked deferred-work ledger. The real fix belongs
# upstream in bmad-loop (write it outside the worktree, or ignore it there); this
# line is the local containment so it cannot reach main again.
claude_hash.txt
# Derived artifact (Story 1.10, AD-12/AD-35): rendered whole from the
# canonical EffectivePolicy by adapters/harness_bmadloop.py on every write --
# never hand-edited, never tracked (closes the F-1 cross-project bleed where
# a loop home's hand-edit rode `git push origin HEAD:main` onto every
# project).
.bmad-loop/policy.toml
# Derived artifact (Story 6.2, AD-12/AD-36): the skill-tree projection
# manifest cli/adapters.py::run_adapters_sync writes per loop home --
# bookkeeping for stale-projection detection only, never hand-edited, never
# tracked (same precedent as .bmad-loop/policy.toml above).
.bmad-loop/skill-projection.json
# Derived artifact (Story 33.3, SPEC-marshal-token-economy CAP-2): the
# wire-compression bmad-loop profile overlay `factory spin` writes per
# adapter when the `wire` layer is on
# (adapters/harness_bmadloop.py::write_spin_wire_profile_overlay). Live gap
# found 2026-09-10: untracked and not ignored, it made `bmad-loop run`
# refuse pyforge-marshal's own loop home with "git worktree is not clean" --
# the same failure shape `.bmad-loop/policy.toml` above already exists to
# prevent. Directory-scoped (not a single filename) because it is
# per-adapter, same precedent as `.bmad-loop/archive/`.
.bmad-loop/profiles/
# pyforge-marshal Story 28.2 (SPEC-marshal-token-economy CAP-2): the
# loop-home-scoped wire-compression (CCR) store the harness-seam wrapper
# writes into. The store lives INSIDE the loop home / dispatch worktree on
# purpose -- that is what makes it torn down with the worktree instead of
# accumulating in a user-global cache -- which puts runtime state in a git
# checkout. Ignored for the same two reasons `.bmad-loop/archive/` and
# `claude_hash.txt` above are: `bmad-loop run` refuses to start on a dirty
# worktree, and the loop's own `git add -A` would otherwise sweep a
# multi-megabyte sqlite cache into a merge commit.
#
# Scoped to `wire/`, NOT to the `.marshal/` namespace: that namespace is the
# Genesis seed subsystem's, and it holds files this repo deliberately leaves
# visible to git -- `.marshal/seed-state.yml`, whose documented remedy for a
# `state-invalid` finding is "Restore ... from version control"
# (`src/shared/packages/pyforge-marshal/docs/finding-remedy-reference.md`),
# and `.marshal/plan.json`. `seed/verbs/adopt.py` already handles its own
# dirty-tree problem by EXCLUDING `.marshal/` with a git pathspec
# (`':!.marshal/'`) rather than ignoring it, so a blanket rule here would
# both shadow a documented recovery path and silently duplicate a mechanism
# that already exists one layer down.
#
# `**/` keeps the any-depth reach the over-broad rule this replaces had: a
# loop home is normally its own worktree root (so this file IS its
# toplevel), but an anchored `.marshal/wire/` would silently stop ignoring
# the store the moment a home sat one directory deeper.
**/.marshal/wire/

# pyforge-marshal Story 28.3 (SPEC-marshal-token-economy CAP-3/CAP-4): the
# other two per-loop-home token-economy kit artifacts Genesis provisions
# (`marshal seed kit --apply`, and `marshal preflight`'s own call to it).
# Ignored for exactly the reason the CCR store above is: both land INSIDE a
# loop home / dispatch worktree by design, `bmad-loop run` refuses to start
# on a dirty worktree, and the loop's own `git add -A` would otherwise sweep
# them into a merge commit. Verified live rather than assumed -- a real
# `marshal seed kit --apply` in a scratch repo leaves `?? .claude/` and
# `?? .codegraph/` in `git status` without these rules.
#
# `**/.claude/skills/caveman/`, NOT `.claude/` and NOT `.claude/skills/`:
# this repo TRACKS `.claude/skills/**` (conda-forge-expert, the pyforge-*
# station skills) and `.claude/settings.json`, so anything broader would
# shadow real source. Only the caveman subdirectory is tool-deployed.
#
# `.codegraph/` ships its own self-ignoring `.gitignore` ("ignore everything
# here except this file"), which is deliberately visible to git -- so the
# index bytes are already ignored, but the directory still shows up
# untracked because of that one file. The rule below is what closes it.
**/.claude/skills/caveman/
**/.codegraph/

# Derived artifact (Story 6.2, AD-12/AD-36): the projected skill tree(s)
# cli/adapters.py::run_adapters_sync creates -- a directory symlink to the
# canonical .claude/skills, never real content, never tracked. Root-anchored
# (mirrors /.herald/ above): .agents/ does not otherwise exist in this repo.
/.agents/
_bmad/_memory/

# Parked artifact-fork evidence dirs (local-only Tier-3 copies; see each dir's README)
_bmad-output/projects/*/_root-fallback-fork-*/

# pyforge-herald: repo-local bridge state (Story 1.4, AD-5) -- the operational
# etag/state store `herald deck` reads and writes, never the source of truth
# for anything git tracks. Root-anchored: AD-5 puts the store at the repo
# root only, and an unanchored pattern would silently swallow any future
# tracked `.herald/` test fixture deeper in the tree.
/.herald/

# The VisualStudio template block above contributes a blanket `*.log`, which
# silently swallowed the conda-forge-expert failure-analyzer's own `.log` test
# fixtures: `tests/fixtures/error_logs/` sat EMPTY and `unmatched.log` could
# never be added, so test_failure_analyzer.py's two unmatched-log cases ran
# against a missing file and asserted on "Log file not found" instead of on the
# no-match contract. Found 2026-08-09 while landing doctor 6.7 -- the same
# failure class as the `/.claude/skills` .git/info/exclude incidents: a broad
# ignore rule hides only NEW files, so `git status` can never show you what it
# is costing. Negated narrowly (this one fixture tree), not by weakening `*.log`.
!.claude/skills/conda-forge-expert/tests/fixtures/error_logs/
!.claude/skills/conda-forge-expert/tests/fixtures/error_logs/**/*.log

# pyforge-steward `sync` duty (Epic 8, Story 8.1): the operator's real
# `.steward/sync-config.yaml` names live GitHub project/field IDs and Jira
# base URL/field IDs for an external board -- not a secret itself, but
# deployment-specific and never meant to be committed to THIS repo (this
# repo only ships the tracked template). Mirrors the `.env`/`.env.example`
# convention above: the example stays tracked, the real file is ignored.
.steward/sync-config.yaml

# pyforge-steward `workspace` duty (Epic 13, Story 13.1): machine-local
# bookkeeping of tool-created scratch worktrees + their archive-not-delete
# tarballs. Never commit — paths are host-absolute and archives hold full
# trees.
.steward/workspaces.yaml
# Story 66.2: the pre-push hook journals every PYFORGE_PREFLIGHT_SKIP=1 here.
.steward/preflight-skips.log
.steward/workspace-archive/
# pyforge-steward `deck-drift` duty (Story 59.4): the machine-local baseline
# sidecar fingerprinting a pulled Design deck artifact (size + sha256) at
# each observed etag -- host-scratch, not repo content.
.steward/deck-integrity-baseline.json

# Fleet-drain / agent scratch worktrees (`git worktree add` under repo root).
# Machine-local checkouts with pixi envs — never commit; remove with
# `git worktree remove` after story merge+finalize.
.worktrees/

# CDO packaging inventory: local consumption workbook + secret gist id.
# Tracked template is conf/conda-forge-packaging-inventory-operations.local.env.example.
docs/Analysis_Dataset-*.xlsx
conf/conda-forge-packaging-inventory-operations.local.env

# Story 11.1: LANGFLOW_CONFIG_DIR/LANGFLOW_KNOWLEDGE_BASES_DIR's local-dev
# default (config/settings/base.py) -- ephemeral runtime scratch (AD-6), same
# category as staticfiles/media, never git-tracked.
src/platform/.langflow/
_bmad/render/

# Story 12.3: scripts/build-pixi-mirror.py's own documented usage example
# (`--dest ci-airgap-mirror`, a relative path at the repo root) -- CI-runtime
# scratch only, hundreds of MB across 428 packages, never git-tracked. A
# developer following that example verbatim locally should not risk
# `git add -A` staging it.
/ci-airgap-mirror/

